---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { PROFILE, SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
                <main id="main">
                        <section class="hero shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
                                <div class="hero-layout">
                                        <div>
                                                <p class="hero-hello">Hello, I'm Samuel.</p>
                                                <h1 id="hero-title">Making things<br />work <em>together.</em></h1>
                                        </div>
                                        <div class="hero-intro">
                                                <span class="hero-symbol" aria-hidden="true">✳</span>
                                                <p>I build the connections between games, identity, and the infrastructure behind them.</p>
                                                <a class="arrow-link" href="#featured">Explore the work <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
                                        </div>
                                </div>
                        </section>

                        <section id="featured" class="featured-section shell" aria-labelledby="featured-title">
                                <div class="featured-project">
                                        <div class="featured-copy">
                                                <div class="feature-label"><span class="feature-dot"></span> Identity &amp; infrastructure</div>
                                                <h2 id="featured-title">HRPAuth<span>.</span></h2>
                                                <p class="feature-lead">One identity. A whole ecosystem.</p>
                                                <p>Built to connect accounts, games, and services, HRPAuth brings authentication and extensible infrastructure together under one roof.</p>
                                                <div class="feature-tags"><span>Go</span><span>OAuth2</span><span>WebAuthn</span><span>Yggdrasil</span></div>
                                                <a class="button button-light" href="https://github.com/CoreMatch/HRPAuth">Explore the source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
                                        </div>
                                        <div class="system-visual">
                                                <div class="system-notes">
                                                        <p class="system-lead">One identity, wired through every surface a player touches.</p>
                                                        <ul class="system-list">
                                                                <li>Web UI</li>
                                                                <li>Game clients</li>
                                                                <li>Services</li>
                                                                <li>Skins &amp; profiles</li>
                                                        </ul>
                                                </div>
                                        </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="feature-details">
                                        <div><p class="label">The idea</p><p>A shared identity foundation for games and the services around them.</p></div>
                                        <div><p class="label">The approach</p><p>OAuth2 and multi-factor authentication meet service discovery and dynamic routing.</p></div>
                                        <div><p class="label">The connection</p><p>Satellite services can contribute frontend capabilities through distributed SDK packages.</p></div>
                                </div>
                        </section>

                        <section id="work" class="work-section shell" aria-labelledby="work-title">
                                <div class="work-heading"><h2 id="work-title">Different ideas.<br /><em>Connected thinking.</em></h2><p>From game servers to simulation engines, each project starts with a problem worth exploring.</p></div>
                                <div class="work-grid">
                                        <article class="work-card"><div class="card-meta">Competitive gaming</div><div class="card-art art-rating" aria-hidden="true"><span>ΔR</span><i>=</i><span>K × (S − E)</span></div><div class="card-body"><h3><a href="/projects#matchcore-arena">MatchCore Arena</a></h3><p>Turning match results into meaningful player ratings, from game-side reporting to the leaderboard.</p><div class="card-tags">Go / ELO / Wails</div></div></article>
                                        <article class="work-card"><div class="card-meta">Game infrastructure</div><div class="card-art art-network" aria-hidden="true"><div class="network-line"></div><span class="network-point point-one"></span><span class="network-point point-two"></span><span class="network-point point-three"></span></div><div class="card-body"><h3><a href="/projects#matchcore-arena">RW-HPS / Go Server</a></h3><p>Exploring a Go-based networking and orchestration layer for Rusted Warfare, with the game kernel kept external.</p><div class="card-tags">Go / Networking / Protocols</div></div></article>
                                        <article class="work-card"><div class="card-meta">Simulation</div><div class="card-art art-simulation" aria-hidden="true"><div class="sim-grid"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div></div><div class="card-body"><h3><a href="/projects#silo40">Silo40</a></h3><p>A configurable organization simulation where roles, traits, and events shape the state of a world.</p><div class="card-tags">Go / Rules engine / Simulation</div></div></article>
                                </div>
                                <a class="all-work-link" href="/projects"><span>There is more to the story.</span><strong>Explore the project directory <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></strong></a>
                        </section>

                        <section class="approach-section" aria-labelledby="approach-title"><div class="shell approach-inner">
                                <div><h2 id="approach-title">Build the pieces.<br /><em>Connect the dots.</em></h2></div>
                                <div class="approach-copy"><p>I like understanding how things fit together: the protocol a client speaks, the service behind it, and the interface that makes it useful.</p><p>These projects are independently developed, with upstream work and reused foundations acknowledged where they belong.</p><a class="arrow-link" href="/about">A little more about me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
                        </div></section>

                        <section id="connect" class="connect-section shell" aria-labelledby="connect-title">
                                <div class="connect-grid"><h2 id="connect-title">Let's make<br /><em>something connect.</em></h2><div><p>Curious about the projects, the code, or the ideas behind them? Find me on GitHub.</p><a class="button button-dark" href={PROFILE.github}>Find Samuel on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div>
                        </section>
                </main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
